    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d415">

                <pb facs="0694" n="624" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg624"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>Mr. Romero to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexican Legation in the United States of
                                America, Washington,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-07-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 27, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Esteemed Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit to
                    you numbers 10 and 11 of the French Moniteur, containing speeches made in the
                    corps legislatif of Paris on the 9th and 10th instant, upon Mexican affairs, by
                    Messrs. Thiers, Favie, and Rouher.</p>
                <p>I also enclose several articles from French papers on the same subject.</p>
                <p>Your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>M. ROMERO.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



















